<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaston de Foix, Duke of Nemours</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1489–1512</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaston de Foix was a French nobleman and commander, nephew of Louis XII, who exchanged his viscounty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a> for the duchy of Nemours in 1507. Leading the French army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1511">Holy League</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a>, he won a series of rapid victories and the Battle of Ravenna on 11 April 1512, but was killed during the pursuit at the age of 22.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaston-de-foix-duke-of-nemours.jpg" alt="Gaston de Foix, Duke of Nemours" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philippe de Champaigne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Gaston_of_Foix,_Duke_of_Nemours_(1489%E2%80%931512),_by_Philippe_de_Champaigne_-_Palace_of_Versailles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
